    privacyIntroduction: "1. Introduction",
    privacyIntro: "This Privacy Policy explains how I, Arkadiy Tsoy (hereinafter \"Developer,\" \"I,\" or \"my\"), collect, use, and protect your personal information when you use the mobile game \"Hwatu\" (hereinafter \"Game\") on iOS and Android. I comply with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA). By using the Game, you agree to the terms of this Privacy Policy.",
    privacyDataCollection: "2. Information I Collect",
    privacyDataCollectionText: "When you use the Game, I may collect the following types of information:",
    privacyAccountInfo: "Account Information: the Game creates an anonymous account for you; there is no sign-up and the Game never asks for your name, email address or photo. If you are signed in to Apple Game Center (iOS) or Google Play Games (Android) on your device, the Game links your account to the player identifier of that service, so that your progress is kept after reinstalling and on your other devices; the Game does not receive your name, email address or photo from it. To use one account on iPhone and on Android, you can link your devices with a one-time code shown in the Game; the code is stored only as a hash and expires after 10 minutes, and the account the other device used before is merged into yours and deleted. Your display name is the one you set in the Game, or, until you set one, a name generated automatically; your avatar is chosen from the Game's own set. Earlier versions of the Game (version 3.0.0 on iOS and test versions on Android) also offered sign-in with Apple or Google. If you used it, your account is linked to that Apple or Google account, and the Game may have received the email address (with Apple, possibly a private relay address) and the name that the sign-in shared. This sign-in is no longer used: after an update, your account is kept by Game Center or Google Play Games. You can remove the Apple or Google sign-in together with that email address and name in later versions of the Game under Profile → “Unlink Apple sign-in” (or Google); they are also removed when you delete your account, and we will remove them from all accounts once the earlier versions are no longer in use.",
