    privacyCloudSave: "9. Cloud Save and Online Features",
    privacyCloudSaveText: "Your progress is stored in the cloud (Google Firebase) under your account. If you are signed in to Game Center or Google Play Games, it can be restored on your other devices and after reinstalling the Game; if you are not, your progress is tied to this device only — sign in to Game Center (iOS) or Google Play Games (Android) to keep it. In online modes and leaderboards, your display name and avatar are visible to other players; the name of your Game Center or Google Play Games account is never shown there, so please do not use personal data in the display name you choose. In online games, other players at the table also see whether you are online. If you stop making moves in an online game or leave it, the Game may make moves for you and give your seat to a computer player.",
    privacyCloudSaveLegacyText: "Earlier versions of the Game for iOS stored progress in Apple iCloud. When you update to the current version, that data is transferred once into the cloud account described above.",
    privacyRetention: "10. Data Retention and Deletion",
    privacyRetentionText: "Account and progress data is kept for as long as your account exists, as are the records of your acceptance of the Terms of Use and this Privacy Policy. Data of an online game (the table, the players' names and avatars, the moves) is deleted within about a day after the game ends; records used to calculate the online rating are deleted after 30 days; messages sent through “Report a problem” are deleted after 180 days. Usage statistics and crash reports are kept according to the standard retention periods of the services listed in section 7. You can delete your account at any time in the Game under Profile → Delete account (at the bottom of the screen; for a guest the item is called “Delete my data”): your account, progress, coins and items, game history, online rating, tournament entries and messages to support are deleted at once, on every device. Records of purchases are kept, so that the same purchase cannot be credited to several accounts; they contain no name or contact details, and their link to the deleted account is removed. Deleting the account does not cancel an active subscription: cancel it in the App Store or Google Play settings, or keep it — it passes to the next game account that you use with the same App Store or Google Play account. You can also ask for deletion by writing to robaya.studio@gmail.com — such requests are processed within 30 days. Deleting the Game from your device does not by itself delete data stored in the cloud; an account that is not linked to Game Center or Google Play Games and has not been used for 12 months is deleted automatically, together with its data, unless it has purchases.",
